---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/marsello-vs-yotpo-email-sms';
const title = 'Marsello vs Yotpo Email & SMS: Shopify continuity (2026)';
const desc = 'Evaluate Marsello for POS and online loyalty, email and SMS; audit continuity after Yotpo Email & SMS decommissioning.';
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is this still a choice between two active senders?",
    "answer": "No. Yotpo Email & SMS is decommissioned. Evaluate Marsello as a current option and treat the Yotpo side as a continuity audit of former messaging, data and obligations."
  },
  {
    "question": "When is Marsello worth evaluating?",
    "answer": "When Shopify and store purchases need a shared loyalty program alongside email and SMS. Prove identity matching, rewards and channel permissions on your own enabled sites before choosing it."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does the shutdown include Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty?",
    "answer": "Keep those products separate from Email & SMS. Inventory your actual Reviews and Loyalty contracts and integrations before changing them; retiring a sender does not itself require replacing a rewards program."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I still export data or port my old number?",
    "answer": "Do not assume dashboard access, exports or number porting remain available. Ask the relevant providers about your account and sender, and work from retained records where access has ended."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does joining loyalty authorize marketing?",
    "answer": "No. Preserve channel-specific permission evidence and suppression status separately from membership and points. Quarantine records whose marketing eligibility cannot be established."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should purchase exits work?",
    "answer": "Use authoritative order events and a fresh eligibility check before delivery. A POS or online purchase should cancel the relevant pending cart or offer job, with retries deduplicated by event and message purpose."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must I add another email provider?",
    "answer": "No. Test whether the chosen platform covers the required journeys and operations. Add a sender only for a demonstrated gap with clear ownership of consent, exclusions and scheduling."
  },
  {
    "question": "How do I compare costs?",
    "answer": "Use the same eligible cohort, period, countries, message segments and loyalty scope. Include platform and usage fees, reward liability, migration labor and support; compare contribution with a holdout rather than attributed sales alone."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is the safe rollback?",
    "answer": "Pause new dispatch, preserve evidence and reconcile queued work and rewards with the operator. Roll back configuration or data mappings only where reversible; a decommissioned sender is not a fallback service."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-14 md:py-20">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a><span> / Marsello vs Yotpo Email &amp; SMS</span></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="badge">Current platform and legacy continuity</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Marsello vs Yotpo Email &amp; SMS for Shopify</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Marsello is a candidate for connecting store and online loyalty with email and SMS. Yotpo Email &amp; SMS has been decommissioned, so this comparison now concerns replacement readiness and retained customer obligations.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl"><TldrBox picks={[
      { label: 'POS and online loyalty', tool: 'Marsello', reason: 'Evaluate enabled sites, rewards and permission sync together' },
      { label: 'Former messaging', tool: 'Yotpo Email & SMS', reason: 'Audit retained evidence and retire legacy jobs; not a new-adoption option' },
      { label: 'Separate products', tool: 'Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty', reason: 'Review their own contracts and integrations independently' }
    ]} /></div>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>What the current evidence supports</h2>
      <p>Checked November 25, 2026: the <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo lifecycle notice</a> says the SMS application is decommissioned and its dashboard and background services are inactive. The <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">2025 migration announcement</a> scheduled Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Historical migration recommendations do not establish current access, export availability or sender portability.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://www.marsello.com/shopify">Marsello’s Shopify page</a> describes loyalty and marketing across eCommerce and connected POS sites. Its <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/how-do-i-connect-my-shopify-site-to-marsello-marsello-help-center">connection documentation</a> describes syncing customers and purchases from enabled sites. Confirm your POS version, sites, market, plan and sender requirements directly. Integration scope is not proof that your historical records will reconcile.</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Marsello evaluation</th><th>Former Yotpo Email &amp; SMS estate</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>New messaging</td><td>Demonstrate required email/SMS journeys and market coverage</td><td>Decommissioned; choose a supported destination</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Customer value</td><td>Test cross-site identity and rewards ledger</td><td>Use retained history only where provenance is known</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Permissions</td><td>Verify channel-specific import and suppression behavior</td><td>Recover evidence from existing archives or confirmed support paths</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Other Yotpo products</td><td>Decide whether rewards replacement is actually required</td><td>Reviews and Loyalty need their own inventory and decision</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <h2>Prove continuity before enabling campaigns</h2>
      <p>Build a mapping from Shopify customer ID and enabled POS site IDs to one destination profile. Normalize phone formats but do not merge people solely because they share a number or email. Resolve duplicate accounts, household contacts and guest checkouts in an exception queue. Keep source IDs and merge decisions so support can explain each balance.</p>
      <p>Reconcile opening points, accrual, expiration, redemption, reserved rewards and return reversals as a ledger, not just a balance import. Test earning online then redeeming in store, the reverse direction, and a partial return after redemption. An approved reversal must apply once even if an event is retried. Reconcile totals and individual exceptions before enabling reward messages.</p>
      <p>Marsello’s <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/how-do-customers-join-my-marsello-database-marsello-help-center">customer joining documentation</a> distinguishes loyalty membership from marketing preferences and notes POS customers need to opt in. Carry source, timestamp, disclosure version, channel and subsequent opt-out evidence into the decision record. Missing evidence means no promotional eligibility until resolved. Preserve email and SMS exclusions with their proper scope; membership and purchase history cannot replace permission.</p>
      <p>Use Shopify order IDs, source site, payment and refund state as order truth. Test out-of-order delivery, a delayed POS sync and purchase during a cart delay. Recheck eligibility just before dispatch and cancel relevant purchase reminders across senders. Key deduplication by source event, customer and message purpose; acknowledge a retry without sending twice.</p>
      <p>Inventory former campaign schedules, flow delays, webhook subscriptions, middleware retries and exported audience jobs. Mark each retired, replaced or quarantined with an owner. The inactive Yotpo service does not prove that external middleware has no queued work. Do not replay a stale cart queue into the new sender. Record a cutover boundary and verify the new sender is the sole owner of each active journey.</p>
      <h2>Proposed merchant fixtures</h2>
      <p>These fictional scenarios preserve distinct campaign jobs for acceptance testing. They are proposed fixtures, not customer results, benchmarks or platform capability claims.</p>
<h3>Ridge Run Coffee</h3>
<p>Suppress active subscribers from a flash offer; a subscription renewal and an ordinary order must produce the correct separate exclusions.</p>
<h3>Arena Energy</h3>
<p>Send a flavor-drop notice only to the relevant interest segment; confirm an email bundle incentive cannot leak into a conflicting SMS offer.</p>
<h3>Loom & Frame</h3>
<p>Trigger a collector notice only after verified edition inventory crosses the chosen threshold; suppress customers who already bought that edition.</p>
<h3>Driftwood Surf Co</h3>
<p>Use a seasonal restock waitlist; a store sale reducing stock must stop an online availability message before dispatch.</p>
<h3>Noir Collective</h3>
<p>Test a weekly frequency cap across email and SMS, including a scheduled VIP drop that collides with a winback delay.</p>
<h3>SoleDrop ATX</h3>
<p>Validate size-specific VIP access and priority order; an exhausted size must not receive a working purchase promise.</p>
<h3>Festival Threads Co</h3>
<p>Use city and recipient timezone for tour notices, including a daylight-saving boundary and a customer traveling between cities.</p>
<h3>Vinyl Vault Records</h3>
<p>Reconcile collector eligibility from POS and online orders without double-counting a returned pressing.</p>
<h3>Bloom & Wick</h3>
<p>Separate gift recipients from purchasers; apply shipping cutoffs to the correct delivery region without assuming gift recipients consented.</p>
<h3>Peak Trail Gear</h3>
<p>Keep clearance incentives out of full-price loyalist journeys and compare net contribution against an eligible holdout.</p>
<h3>Sauce Lab</h3>
<p>Use batch-level inventory for a scarcity notice; replay the same stock event and prove only one eligible message is queued.</p>
<h3>Ember Ceramics</h3>
<p>Preserve waitlist priority for a small kiln release; do not migrate old queued invitations as fresh entitlements.</p>
<h3>Cipher Audio</h3>
<p>Test a teaser-to-launch journey with no assumed discount; purchase between stages must cancel the launch reminder.</p>
<h3>Patchwork Denim</h3>
<p>Match style preferences to one-of-one listings; sale at the POS must retire the listing and pending messages everywhere.</p>
      <h2>Matched costs and contribution</h2>
      <p>Request a current quote for the same enabled sites, eligible profiles, countries, SMS segments, email volume and loyalty scope. Include carrier charges, overages, integration labor, support, reward liability and any remaining separate Reviews or Loyalty contract. A retired product’s historical price is not a competing live quote.</p>
      <p>Hypothetical pilot: 1,000 eligible customers produce $6,000 net sales after discounts and returns, less $2,400 goods, $600 fulfillment, $200 messaging/platform allocation and $300 operator labor: $2,500 contribution, or $2.50 per eligible customer. A matched 1,000-customer holdout contributes $2,100 after its comparable costs, so estimated lift is $400, or $0.40 per eligible customer. Do not subtract discounts or refunds twice. Charge a hypothetical $800 migration separately: first-period lift after that cost is negative $400. These inputs illustrate the calculation, not expected results.</p>
      <h2>Operator handoff and rollback</h2>
      <p>Name an owner for profile exceptions, ledger adjustments, permission disputes, sender replies and campaign release. Give support a source-to-destination lookup, reconciliation report, retired-job list and escalation contacts. Release a small eligible cohort only after the order, opt-out, redemption and retry fixtures pass. Set pause thresholds for duplicate dispatch, unexplained balances or missing exclusions before launch.</p>
      <p>If a threshold fails, pause dispatch, retain event logs and reconcile changes before resuming. Restore reversible mappings from the approved snapshot where appropriate; never erase valid opt-outs or replay completed rewards. A decommissioned sender cannot serve as rollback capacity. Confirm any remaining archive retrieval or number-transfer options with the providers rather than promising them to operators.</p>
      <p>Choose Marsello conditionally when its demonstrated POS/online loyalty and marketing workflow fits the team. Keep a different supported sender or separate loyalty service when the pilot reveals a specific gap. Use the <a class="link" href="/apps/marsello">Marsello profile</a>, <a class="link" href="/apps/yotpo-email-sms">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS profile</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">cost worksheet</a> for related context.</p>
    </article>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Marsello vs Yotpo Email & SMS FAQ" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
